ernal market in the area of  cybersecurity it's also important for  consumers for European citizens because  they will know the level at which  security corresponds to whatever they're  purchasing now what comes next to the  Commissioner is going to launch a an all  stakeholder call to create a group of  experts for certification we are going  to initiate consultations with a view to  preparing the union's work program this  work program was set up priorities for  certification for the coming years now  with the cybersecurity act once it's  come into force will then have the  proposal for the European competence our  Skills Center for cybersecurity now this  is a proposal which as you know has  already been debated during to try Logue  sessions with both European Parliament  and the council we will be working  towards a political agreement on this  file by the end of October in addition  to cybersecurity ladies and gentlemen  I'm also happy to be able to announce  new developments to you today with  regard to our European strategy for the  development of artificial intelligence  in April we welcomed the fact that the  conditions were in place for in  artificial intelligence centred on  humans and worthy of trust this was a  set of guidelines proposed by our  high-level expert group now the group  has also suggested an evaluation list of  a practical nature to allow parties our  stakeholders to verify whether the  principles in the guidelines  comply with these conditions so from  today on companies and all of other all  of the other stakeholders will be in a  position to test the actual  implementation  in reality of this evaluation list so  call upon everybody involved in AI to  share their experience with us and to  get involved in this pilot phase which  will continue until December we are  talking here about very useful  information because the analysis will be  in a position to be presented at the  beginning of 2020 all the information on  this initiative can b